WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
If your prep is SuTab, this video will walk you through exactly how to take

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:03.920
it.

3
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.320
Just follow along step by step. Your SuTab kit includes two bottles of 12

4
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:08.880
tablets each

5
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.700
and a measured container. Start your first dose between 6 and 7 PM the night

6
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.560
before your procedure.

7
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:19.800
Open your first bottle of 12 tablets. Fill the provided container with 16

8
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:20.560
ounces of water up

9
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.120
to the fill line. Swallow one tablet every 2 minutes with a sip of water,

10
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:25.920
finishing all 12

11
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:30.560
tablets over about 15 to 20 minutes. Take your time and go at a steady pace.

12
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.640
About 1 hour after

13
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.770
your last tablet, fill the container again with 16 ounces of water and drink

14
00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:37.760
the entire amount

15
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:43.010
slowly over 30 minutes. Then, about 30 minutes after finishing that container,

16
00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:43.680
fill it one more

17
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.180
time with 16 ounces of water and drink the entire amount over 30 minutes. That

18
00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.200
completes your first

19
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:54.830
dose. 7 hours prior to your procedure, repeat the exact same three steps

20
00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:56.160
using your second bottle

21
00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:01.060
of 12 tablets. One tablet every 2 minutes with water, then 16 ounces of water

22
00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.080
one hour later,

23
00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.880
then 16 ounces of water 30 minutes after that. This part is really important.

24
00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:07.680
You must drink

25
00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.600
all of the prep solution as directed, even if you're already passing clear

26
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:11.840
liquid.

27
00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.240
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

28
00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:16.720
the clearest

29
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.860
view during your procedure. If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may

30
00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:22.000
need to reschedule,

31
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.130
and neither of us wants that. Between doses, keep drinking clear liquids to

32
00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:27.040
stay hydrated.

33
00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.160
It will help you feel better and help the prep do its job. Do not drink

34
00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:31.840
anything at all within

35
00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:35.710
4 hours of your procedure, including water, unless it is a small sip to take

36
00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:36.560
a medication.

37
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.320
Your procedure may be canceled or rescheduled if this is not followed. If you

38
00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:42.080
experience any

39
00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.800
discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom, applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper

40
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:53.220
rash cream can really help. That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing,

41
00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:54.080
finish the full dose,

42
00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:58.480
and stay hydrated. If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our

43
00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.960
office. We're here to help.
